# Testing with Playwright

Docs: https://playwright.dev/docs/intro and https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/testing/

## Suites

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `tests/e2e/smoke.spec.ts` | Home page renders, document basics, no console errors or hydration warnings, skip link is the first tab stop and moves focus to `main`, tab order reaches every visible control in DOM order without a trap (a radio group is one stop: its checked radio), the page stays light (same colours, `color-scheme: light only`) whether the device prefers light or dark |
| `tests/e2e/a11y.spec.ts` | Every built page: axe-core scan with WCAG 2.2 A/AA tags, zero violations (automated subset only) |
| `tests/e2e/motion.spec.ts` | `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` turns off smooth scrolling and leaves no running animation; motion is allowed otherwise |
| `tests/e2e/seo.spec.ts` | Every built page: title and description lengths, canonical, `lang`, one viewport meta, one `h1`, image `alt`, valid JSON-LD |
| `tests/e2e/layout.spec.ts` | Every built page at 360, 390, 768, 1024, 1440, and 1920 px: no horizontal overflow, no element past the viewport, no clipped text, `h1` in view; writes screenshots to `reports/screenshots/`. Runs under reduced motion and loads every lazy image before each screenshot, so sections show at rest (a full-page capture never scrolls, so the work props would otherwise sit tucked behind their cards and lazy photos show empty) |
| `tests/e2e/rendering.spec.ts` | Sitemap, robots, favicons served; unknown routes return 404; every internal link on every page resolves |
| `tests/e2e/navigation.spec.ts` | Navbar: every `primaryNav` entry and the call to action render, only entries with an `href` are links, the current page is marked; below `lg` the links collapse into a menu dialog that opens from the keyboard, closes with Escape, the close button, a scrim click, or a resize to desktop, returns focus to the menu button, and passes axe while open |
| `tests/e2e/hero.spec.ts` | Home hero: headline, copy, and buttons are HTML (the primary follows `primaryCta`, About us targets `#about`); the device image is eager, `fetchpriority="high"`, and sized; the pencil underline is the only animation on load, plays once (200-300 ms delay, 700-900 ms) and stays drawn, is finished at once under reduced motion, is `aria-hidden`, and stays under its phrase at 360-1440 px; the buttons have no transitions; the primary's aura stays unlit with its spin paused until the pointer reaches it, then the navbar's endless light (same animation and timing) fades in; when the pointer leaves the light fades out and the spin stays paused where it stopped, and the next hover continues from there; nothing under reduced motion, and it takes no room of its own at 390 and 1280 px |
| `tests/e2e/introduction.spec.ts` | Home introduction: the copy ends with the primary "Learn more" button (a link only once `aboutCta.href` is set), whose visually hidden words make its name "Learn more about Auralink Studio"; it sits under the text and in line with it, 32px below on phones and 48px from 768px, with an 18px label, as Hub2B's "Read more" does; it changes colour without transitions, and its aura stays unlit until the pointer reaches it, fades out when the pointer leaves, and continues from where the spin stopped |
| `tests/e2e/services.spec.ts` | Home services section: introduction ending with the primary "View all services" button (a link only once `servicesCta.href` is set) and one card per `serviceCards` entry with an `aria-hidden` inline SVG icon; the cards cover the service catalogue exactly once; one, two, then four columns, with the introduction in the first two cells from xl (the Hub2B arrangement); every card keeps the Hub2B tile look (white, square, borderless, centred, a 96px primary icon) and fades in its 2px primary frame under the pointer (at once under reduced motion) without moving; renders without JavaScript; each card links where `src/lib/service-cards.ts` says, or has no link, label, or arrow and ignores the pointer. Linked cards (skipped with a reason while no destination exists): the arrow shows before hover, Tab and Enter work with a visible ring, hover or keyboard focus slides the arrow 3-4px without moving any card, never under reduced motion |
| `tests/e2e/work.spec.ts` | Home selected work: filters by platform (`workFilters`) as a radio group in a fieldset named "Show the projects built with", opening on the first; each shows only its own project, by click, by the arrow keys (Tab reaches the group, with a 2px ring on the pill), and without JavaScript; the other projects stay in the HTML but out of sight and the accessibility tree. Each card has its platform label, description, `aria-hidden` feature icons, and an `aria-hidden` number 01-03, and one link to the supplied address in a new tab, named by its visible label ("View website", "View demo", "View store") plus visually hidden words giving the project name and "opens in a new tab", described by the note under it where the site asks for a password: "Demo password: …" with the password bold and `translate="no"` when the owner has published it, otherwise "Password protected"; Tab goes from the filters to the visible card's link, with the 2px ring. Photos are lazy, 3:2, and fetched at the width `sizes` gives at six widths; from xl the copy fills the left third and the photo the rest, flush top and right, below xl the copy comes first; the number sits under the photo; every card fills the panels, so switching never changes the height. Props: two decorative images under each card (empty alt), resting 45% above and 40% below it, inside its width. Pop-out (`src/lib/reveal.ts`, `pop-out`): tucked behind the card below the fold at load, out over 1s with `ease` once in view and after loading, again for each filter, with no box moved and no layout shift; never moving without JavaScript, under reduced motion, or when on screen at load, even as the stylesheet arrives (no `transitionrun`) |
| `tests/e2e/routes.ts`, `tests/e2e/console.ts` | Helpers: routes from `dist/` (call inside tests), console and hydration-warning capture |

## Engine and viewport matrix

| Project | Device profile | Runs |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `desktop-chromium` | Desktop Chrome 1280x720 | all suites, including `seo`, `layout`, `rendering` |
| `desktop-firefox` | Desktop Firefox 1280x720 | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `hero`, `introduction`, `services`, `work` |
| `desktop-webkit` | Desktop Safari 1280x720 | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `hero`, `introduction`, `services`, `work` |
| `mobile-chromium` | Pixel 7 emulation | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `hero`, `introduction`, `services`, `work` |
| `mobile-webkit` | iPhone 15 emulation | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `hero`, `introduction`, `services`, `work` |

Engine-independent suites (metadata, static assets, viewport layout) run once in desktop Chromium on purpose; do not add them to the other projects. Mobile projects are browser emulations, not physical devices.

## Running

- Routine: `npm run test:e2e:chromium` (desktop and mobile Chromium).
- Full matrix: `npm run test:e2e` (rebuilds `dist/` first, serves it on port 4322).
- One suite or project: `npx playwright test tests/e2e/layout.spec.ts --project=desktop-chromium`.
- Debug: `npm run test:e2e:ui`; last report: `npm run test:e2e:report`.
- Against an existing build without rebuilding: `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_BUILD=1 npx playwright test`.
- Browsers are installed once with `npx playwright install chromium firefox webkit`.
- The web server command is `astro preview --port 4322 --ignore-lock`: Astro 7 would otherwise detach the server into the background when run by an agent, and Playwright could not stop it. Keep the flag and the port (4321 is the dev server).

## Engine notes

- WebKit mirrors Safari: plain Tab skips links. Tests that must reach a link in WebKit press `Alt+Tab` (Option+Tab); this is engine behaviour, not a site defect.
- Playwright's WebKit is newer than the Safari visitors run, so it can pass where Safari fails: Safari 27.2 left the navbar call to action's aura lit after the pointer left, from a repaint bug WebKit fixed on 2026-10-09. Check paint and motion changes in Safari itself, and test the mechanism where the engine cannot show the bug (the navigation suite's "fades through its strength" test).
- A Playwright WebKit screenshot breaks a running transition of an `@property` custom property: afterwards the computed value reads the end value while the transition still runs, so the shot shows a finished fade. Sample such fades with `getComputedStyle` across animation frames, or record a video, not with screenshots.
- Firefox is Playwright's bundled build. On macOS 27.2 it fails to start ("Could not find profile folder") with or without a sandbox; run the rest of the matrix with `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_FIREFOX=1 npm run test:e2e`, then run Firefox in the Linux container described in `docs/quality-checks.md`, or state in the report that Firefox ran only in CI (Ubuntu). Never skip it silently.
- CI runs on Linux, which still differs from macOS: WebKit styles the page once before the stylesheet arrives, and before Catamaran and Mukta load the generic fallback is DejaVu Sans. After those files load, both platforms draw the same families. A macOS pass does not show that CI passes; reproduce platform-specific failures in the Linux container.

## Writing tests

- Add a focused spec for each new interactive island or form (`tests/e2e/<feature>.spec.ts`). Page-level metadata, layout, and accessibility are already covered by the site-wide suites, so do not duplicate those assertions.
- Locate elements by role and accessible name (`getByRole('button', { name: /send/i })`), then by label or text. Avoid CSS selectors tied to Tailwind classes.
- Use web-first assertions (`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()`); never `waitForTimeout`.
- Test behaviour visible to the user: navigation opens and closes with keyboard, form validation messages appear and are associated with fields, filters change the list. Do not test third-party services; for Netlify Forms assert the hidden `form-name` input and attributes instead of submitting.
- Keep tests independent and deterministic; no shared mutable state between tests.
- Mark temporary skips with a reason: `test.skip(condition, 'reason')`, and remove them before finishing.

## Screenshots

`reports/screenshots/` holds inspection screenshots written by the layout suite and by manual checks. They are gitignored and are not visual-regression baselines; look at them and describe what you saw. If visual regression testing is adopted later, baselines must be reviewed on every change, never regenerated to make a failure disappear.

## When a check fails

Read the failing step's name (route, width, or action), reproduce locally with `--ui` if needed, fix the page rather than loosening the assertion. Thresholds in the SEO, layout, and accessibility suites change only with a documented decision in `docs/quality-checks.md`.
